<title>UK: London tea auction sees African origins firm.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees African origins firm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's London tea auction saw healthy buying interest in Central and East African origins with prices tending firmer, the official report said.</p>
<p>Ceylons sold well at steady rates in good overall demand for landed teas.</p>
<p>Offshore teas met with good competition at firm rates, the report said.</p>
<p>The next sale is on Monday, February 10. --London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
